-- title:
--   Flatness at p∤ N of a Hecke–Galois datum's representation
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N\neq 0$, a finite set $S\subseteq\mathbb{N}$, a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}$ (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal) of characteristic zero with finite residue field, a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the Hecke algebra $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\ N\ 2\ S$ — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, and a complete local Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $T$ that is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, with local structure map. Assume $p$ is a prime, $p\neq 2$, the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, $p\nmid N$, $p\in S$, and every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$. Let $H$ be a `HeckeGaloisRepDatum` for these data, so $H$ consists of a ring homomorphism $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $T$ lifting $\theta$ on residue fields, with $\mathcal{O}$-algebra generated by its image, satisfying the point-lifting property for characters reducing to $\theta$ and with $T$'s residue field generated by that of $\mathcal{O}$, together with a rank-two adically continuous representation $\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ are $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. The conclusion is that $\rho$ is flat at $p$: the residue field of $T$ is finite and, for every ideal $I\subseteq T$ with $T/I$ finite, there is a commutative ring $H'$ carrying a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, finite and flat over that subring, and a bijection from the set of its algebra homomorphisms into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (with its convolution monoid structure) onto $\rho.V/I\rho.V$ carrying the convolution product to addition and commuting with the Galois actions.
--
--   This is the flat local condition at a residue characteristic $p$ prime to the level: the torsion quotients of the Hecke–Galois representation come from finite flat group schemes over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. It is used in assembling the local conditions of the deformation problem and in the $R=T$ statements for the Hecke algebra localised at a residual eigenvalue system.
